;; Math (owner L12): the names of java.lang.Math that Clojure code writes (stdlib §4.10, §4.16; only
;; Math/abs is tranche 1, the rest of the module is tranche 4). It is `:require`d with its own name,
;; (:require [Math :as Math]), and used as (Math/abs x); the Java class names become implicit aliases
;; only with E15. Not under fib.*: it is a Java name, so after the flip it takes no implicit :use
;; (plan §4.1) and the one it needs is written here.
;;
;; Decided here: abs is fib.core's (L1: generic over Num, Ord and Unit, so every width and both float widths
;; work), reached by its qualified name because the module's own `abs` shadows it. It traps on the minimum of
;; an integer type (the neg overflows: `integer overflow in neg at i64`, where Java's Math.abs returns the
;; minimum); and it gives 0.0 for -0.0 and NaN for NaN, as Java does, which a bare (if (< x 0) (neg x) x)
;; does not for the first (case 654).
;;
;; Package LIB-2: sqrt pow floor ceil round random log are fib.math's (stdlib §4.10 rows Math/sqrt Math/pow Math/floor Math/ceil
;; Math/round Math/random Math/log). A program that requires Math links libm only through them (the emitter prunes the rest).
(ns Math (:use fib.core) (:require [fib.math :as m]))

(defun abs (x: t) :where ((Num t) (Ord t) (Unit t)) -> t (fib.core/abs x))

(defun sqrt (x: f64) -> f64 (m/sqrt x))
(defun pow (a: f64 b: f64) -> f64 (m/pow a b))
(defun floor (x: f64) -> f64 (m/floor x))
(defun ceil (x: f64) -> f64 (m/ceil x))
(defun round (x: f64) -> i64 (m/round x))
(defun random () -> f64 (m/random))
(defun log (x: f64) -> f64 (m/log x))
